CLIENT STYLE:
Warm, generous, family hospitality.
Autumn gatherings: long tables, copper trays, soft evening light.

CLIENT RULES FOR THE PHOTOGRAPH (these override the reference and the brief):
ALWAYS: the brass tray stays in view
NEVER: no cutlery

THE CLIENT'S OWN IMAGE RULES (they stand above every default about realism, light, people and product fidelity; the set, composition and scale still follow the picked style or the grid tile):
Every box keeps its printed lid.

PHOTOGRAPHY DIRECTION (the lens, light and angle of every picture of this brand; the picked style or grid tile keeps its set and composition): 50mm, eye level, soft window light.

REFERENCE SHOT: this post recreates the place, camera, framing and gesture of one picture of the reference, with new faces for any people: Low side light across a marble table, one hand lifting a piece.
The client's product is shown the way it is really held or served: a box or tin held level with both hands from below or set on a surface, a tray on a table, one piece lifted between the fingers; it is never squeezed into the reference's cup, cup carrier, glass, wrapper or plate, never put into a bag, and never cut out and pasted onto the scene.

PROPS: none this month. Add no decorations of your own (no geometric blocks, cubes, pedestals, beads, pearls scattered around, fabric accents, ribbons, leaves, flowers or petals): the picture holds the surface, the product, the people the post names and what its idea itself needs.

FORMAT: a portrait post frame; the subject fills it with comfortable margins. Nothing important touches the edges; no bars, borders or collage.

HEADLINE SPACE: keep roughly a third of the frame as a calm, low-contrast, low-detail area (plain surface, soft sky, blurred depth) where a headline can be placed later. The subject stays sharp in the rest of the frame.

PALETTE: the scene, props, surfaces and light sit inside this palette: Cream #f3e9d2, Pistachio #7a9a5a. The product, its packaging and print keep the exact colours of its photo; packaging is never recoloured to match the palette.

NO PRODUCT PHOTO: no product photo is attached to this post, so no packaged product, box, tin, tray of sweets, label or brand item appears anywhere; nothing is invented to stand in for one, and no product name or word is written on anything.

TEXT: the image contains no letters, numbers, words, logos, labels, stickers, price tags, watermarks, speech bubbles or user-interface elements, in any language or script. Headlines, prices and logos are added later outside the image. Where the product itself carries printed text on its packaging in image 1, that packaging is reproduced exactly as photographed, nothing else is written anywhere.

FULL FRAME: the photograph fills the entire canvas edge to edge in the requested aspect ratio. When that ratio differs from the model photo's, the scene is extended and re-framed to fill the canvas (more setting to the sides or above and below), never padded. No white or coloured bars, borders, margins, mats, frames, letterboxing or pillarboxing, no picture-inside-a-picture, no polaroid or print edges; if a reference photo carries such bars, they are not part of the scene and are never reproduced.

PHOTOGRAPHY: a very realistic high-end commercial product photograph, as shot by a professional food and product photographer on a full-frame camera with a macro-capable lens: the product is the sharp hero with true-to-life texture, crumbs, sheen and printing; real materials, natural depth of field, honest colour and contrast; never a 3D render, CGI, illustration or AI-smooth look. The light has one clear source and direction and every object casts a shadow consistent with it.

SHADOWS: one light source for the whole scene. Every object, the product included, casts exactly one shadow consistent in direction, length and softness with that light, with a soft contact shadow at its base; nothing floats, nothing has a second shadow or a shadow from a light that is not in the scene.

PEOPLE: none. No person, model, face, body, crowd or silhouette appears, whatever the style reference shows. At most one natural hand holding or placing the product, and only when the post asks for it.

MISTAKES SEEN IN EARLIER PICTURES FOR THIS CLIENT (the review rejected them; never repeat any of them):
- The product is never shown in a bag.

PHOTO ONLY: the image is a plain photograph, not a designed post. No logo, brand mark, emblem, header or footer band, ornamental strip, pattern border, frame or graphic panel is drawn anywhere: the designer adds the logo and graphics afterwards. Brand patterns appear only where they are printed on the product's own packaging in its photo.

AVOID: people toasting or clinking cups or glasses together ('cheers'), text, letters, numbers, logos, watermarks, price tags, UI elements, speech bubbles, extra limbs, duplicated products, a cup or drink inside a plate or bowl, changed product colour or shape, toppings or garnish the product photo does not show, other food or drinks, people who are not in the post, borders or bars, collage, split frames, cartoon, CGI or illustration style unless the brief asks for it, oversaturated HDR, plastic skin."
`;

